{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278952-exemplary-titans","id":1278952,"title":"Exemplary Titans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-06T06:13:14-08:00","id":1278952,"title":"Exemplary Titans","content":"Scion 2E made definition of Titan much more fluid and not obvious on first sight. It gives Storyguides more means for different stories \u2013 but also leaves starting Storyguides on wondering who should be a Titan in their stories. This topic is for pointing obvious and not so obvious candidates from each Pantheon. I will collect in this post on editing few times a month.<br /> <br /> I split list in to two variants:<br /> <b>Titan</b> \u2013 being that is real Titan and probably enemy of gods all the time.<br /> <b>Titan-to-be</b> \u2013 \u2018mad\u2019 or \u2018problematic\u2019 gods that in right circumstances can become proper Titans. For now they are tolerated in Pantheon, but are source of at least few problems for their brothers and sisters. Part of all Incarnation of particular god can be 'malevolent' - where rest of Incarnations of it can even try to stop the previous ones and help whole Pantheon in it!<br /> <br /> <b>Aesir</b><br /> <br /> Titans of Aesir are Giants, known as J\u00f6tnar \u2013 so any being marked as this category is fair Titan in Scion games.<ul><li><b>Surtr </b>\u2013 devil-giant with the flaming sword, Surtr, who will bring forth the flames that engulf the World during the Twilight of the Gods.</li> <li><b>Loki </b>\u2013 being half-J\u00f6tnar points they to possible Titan role. Being father and mother to many monsters also points him in this direction. But the fated betrayal of Aesir and help in starting Ragnarok is direct pointing that he can be seen as Titan-to-be.</li> </ul><b>Bogi ( Bogovi in 1E )</b><ul><li><b>Morena </b>\u2013 Goddes of Winter and Death is cold as ice and stealing humans in the dark winter days is clearly a Titan.</li> <li><b>Chors </b>\u2013 \u2018mad\u2019 Moon God/dess, with army of monstrous children at his/her disposal is good candidate for Titan-to-be.</li> </ul><b>Deva</b><br /> <br /> <b>Kami</b><br /> <br /> <b>Manitou</b><br /> <br /> <b>Netjet</b><br /> <br /> <b>Orisha</b><br /> <br /> <b>Shen</b><br /> <br /> <b>Teotel</b><ul><li><b>Cipacti</b> - definitely a Titan, if she wasn't already; as a primal monster of the deeps, her ghost is probably still around to return the World to her old ocean.</li> <li><b>Itzpapalotl</b> \u2013 Titan-to-be as the Tzitzimime Queen, since they are prophesied to be the destroyers of the world regardless of their fondness towards humanity when the sun goes out. It's nothing personal, it's just who she is<b>.</b></li> </ul><b>Theoi</b><br /> <br /> <b>Tuatha De Danann</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-07-2019, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T07:06:56-08:00","id":1278962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278952-exemplary-titans#post1278952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Chors </b>\u2013 \u2018mad\u2019 Moon God/dess, with army of monstrous children at his/her disposal is good candidate for Titan-to-be.</div> </div> </div> </div>What monstrous children? And where are you getting the &quot;mad&quot; bit from? I thought we had pretty much just the name and some speculation for Chors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T07:53:34-08:00","id":1278965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278952-exemplary-titans?p=1278962#post1278962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What monstrous children? And where are you getting the &quot;mad&quot; bit from? I thought we had pretty much just the name and some speculation for Chors?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278397-2e-bogovi-slavic-pantheon?p=1278967#post1278967\">Moving answer on this</a> to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278397-2e-bogovi-slavic-pantheon\">[2E] Bogovi - Slavic Pantheon</a> topic, where it's place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-06-2019, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https: